# api/ — SvelteKit web-app environment (example / NON-SECRET template)
#
# SCOPE: the SvelteKit app's local-dev env template — the file a dev copies to
# `api/.env` (gitignored). SvelteKit loads `.env` from THIS directory (the app
# root), so it holds the app's NON-SECRET runtime vars of BOTH shapes:
#   • $env/dynamic/PUBLIC (PUBLIC_-prefixed) — shipped to the browser (e.g. the
#     anon key: RLS-scoped, browser-safe, NOT a secret).
#   • $env/dynamic/PRIVATE — server-read, NOT browser-exposed but still NON-SECRET
#     (e.g. PLAID_ENV, the Plaid API-tier selector driving the CSP connect-src host).
# In production Coolify injects these at runtime.
#
# HARD INVARIANT — SECRETS NEVER GET REAL VALUES HERE. The service-role key,
# WORKER_ADMISSION_SHARED_SECRET, PLAID_SECRET, etc. are confined to THIS
# container's own SECRETS section below (never real values in this repo) +
# Coolify injection at runtime — see api/docker-compose.yaml's `app.environment`
# block, the actual production contract (this file documents its NAMES only).
# service_role in particular is confined to the 3 RT-26 allowlist endpoints (Plaid
# webhook / public_token exchange / item remove) and never touches the auth
# chokepoint. Non-secret ≠ secretless-of-consequence: keep this file secret-free.
#
# NON-SECRET here ⇒ NOT a secrets-manifest.yml entry (the manifest governs only the
# CI/prod NON-OVERLAP of actual SECRETS; non-secret config is out of its scope —
# same rule as WORKER_ADMISSION_URL + the worker's own PLAID_ENV). NB
# WORKER_ADMISSION_URL is deliberately NOT declared below either (F/CTO ruling
# 2026-09-20, root .env.example retirement, N-shape check): it is not in
# api/docker-compose.yaml's `app.environment` block (Coolify never injects it —
# the code default in each admissionClient.ts/syncClient.ts IS correct in
# production; the env var exists only as a local/CI override), so declaring it
# here would break this file's own fenced bidirectional-equality property
# against that block (scripts/ci/fence-app-env-template.sh).
#
# Copy to `.env` (gitignored) and fill in for local dev.

PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=
PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=

# $env/dynamic/PRIVATE, non-secret (see header). Plaid API-tier selector; name matches
# the worker's `z.enum(['sandbox','production']).default('sandbox')` so one value drives
# both the worker's Plaid client and the CSP connect-src host. Non-'production' → sandbox.
PLAID_ENV=sandbox

# --- SECRETS — Coolify-injected at runtime, NEVER set in api/.env -----------
# F/CTO ruling 2026-09-20 (root .env.example retirement): this container's
# SECRETS contract used to live in a SEPARATE repo-root `.env.example`
# (`git rm`'d in the same change) — that file is gone; this section is now
# the single, canonical enumeration of this surface's secrets. Each name
# below is pushed onto THIS Coolify application's OWN env store by a
# separate script (never hardcoded, never read from a local `.env` in
# production) — see api/docker-compose.yaml's own `ENV —` header comment for
# the exact minting script per name and docs/deployment-runbook.md §7.1 step 1
# for the numbered push procedure. Leave these BLANK here — a real value in
# a local `api/.env` is never read in production and would only risk a
# leaked secret sitting in a gitignored-but-still-on-disk local file.
#   SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY       — RT-26-allowlisted §4.1 server-source
#     surface only (ADR-016); minted by scripts/mint-supabase-jwt-keys.sh.
#   PDF_WORKER_SIGNING_KEY          — signs/verifies the short-lived PDF
#     worker JWT (SD-20 / RT-21); SAME value on the PDF worker (see
#     workers/pdf-render/.env.example); pushed by
#     scripts/push-production-secrets.sh.
#   WORKER_ADMISSION_SHARED_SECRET  — authenticates this app's relay POST to
#     the provider-sync worker's internal admission endpoint (SELF-212
#     Option-C, C6-2); SAME value on that worker (see
#     workers/provider-sync/.env.example); pushed by
#     scripts/push-production-secrets.sh.
#   DISCORD_WEBHOOK_URL             — outbound Coolify→Discord notification
#     dispatch; pushed by scripts/push-production-secrets.sh.
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=
PDF_WORKER_SIGNING_KEY=
WORKER_ADMISSION_SHARED_SECRET=
DISCORD_WEBHOOK_URL=
